Exactly.  Things that you set aside until "later" aren't particularly
broken, because as "later" gets later, you end up having more and more
resources to where you can finish the game anyway -- and now it's just
personal preference how you can approach it.  

Getting some good +5 armor early in the game is always nice, of course, 
but it's not as safe as it used to be to convert altars, and then of
course you do have to contend with the possibility of getting an orcish
bow or the like.  And as you go up in level, it becomes more and more
difficult to get the gifts instead of artifacts -- so you have to get to
something early or forgo the opportunity entirely.

(Put another way, you're making a far better argument that polypiling is
a problem rather than the armor itself -- the ability to consistently 
create everything you need, regardless of the raw materials actually 
found, is a significant unbalancing factor and always has been.  I
haven't seen much need to change it yet, but that doesn't mean I don't
keep a close eye on it.  hcobb spends a lot of time outlining strategies
that seem to result in a lot of Rogue bones with Magicbane on his machine; 
I'm really not concerned about strategies that leave bones being broken.)

